It is Wednesday evening and I am walking home from the bus stop.
I stop at the local vegetable market on the way.
Now buying vegetables is a normal part of my week.
I see fresh vegetables on a cart.
I say hello to the vegetable vendor.
"Hello bhaiya, how are you?" I ask.
He smiles and says, "I am fine, madam."
"What do you need today?"
I point towards the tomatoes and onions.
"Please give me one kilo of tomatoes and half a kilo of onions," I say.
"Okay, madam."
"Do you need anything else?" bhaiya asks.
I see some fresh green coriander and green chillies.
"Yes, please give me some coriander and a little green chilli too."
He weighs the vegetables and puts them in my cloth bag.
"How many rupees is it in total?" I ask him.
"Eighty rupees, madam," he says.
I give him a hundred-rupee note.
He returns twenty rupees to me.
"Thank you, bhaiya," I say.
I walk towards my building.
The smell of fresh vegetables rises from the bag.
